Sleevenotes packs — licence
===========================

There are two layers here and they are not licensed alike. Read both, because
the first one is more permissive than people expect and the second is narrower
than it might look.


1. The record data: public domain
---------------------------------

Every fact in these files — who played, on what instrument, on which release,
under which label, on what date — comes from the Discogs monthly data dump,
which Discogs publishes under the CC0 1.0 Universal Public Domain Dedication:

    "This data is made available under the CC0 No Rights Reserved license"
    https://data.discogs.com/

CC0 puts the data in the public domain. It carries no attribution requirement
and no conditions, and nothing in this file adds any. We could not restrict it
if we wanted to, and we do not want to: the facts about who was in a room in
1938 belong to everybody.

So: take the personnel, take the dates, take the credits. You need no
permission from us for any of it.


2. The compilation: CC BY-SA 4.0
--------------------------------

What is ours is the layer on top of those facts, and it is a real layer:

  * which records are in a pack and which are not — the scope of a subject,
    and the era boundaries drawn around it;
  * which pressing of a recording is the one shown, chosen once across every
    pack so that two packs never disagree about the same tune;
  * the arrangement: the card shape, the field set, the confidence tiers, the
    pack plan and the manifest that describes it.

That selection and arrangement is licensed under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence:

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

In short: use it, including commercially, provided you credit Sleevenotes and
licence any work derived from the compilation under the same terms.

This is deliberately a thin claim, and it is meant to be honest about how thin
it is. It does not reach the underlying facts, which are CC0 and stay CC0. If
you rebuild an equivalent corpus from the Discogs dump yourself, you owe us
nothing at all.


3. The software is not covered here
-----------------------------------

The Sleevenotes application and the ingest pipeline that produced these files
are separate work, are not distributed in this branch, and are not licensed by
this file.


Attribution
-----------

    Sleevenotes packs — https://sleevenotes.ink
    Compilation licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
    Record data from Discogs, CC0

See ATTRIBUTION.md for what is in these files, where each field came from, and
what is deliberately not here.
